The function below title-cases whitespace-delimited words in each record. Unicode whitespace characters must be preserved exactly. At the start of each record and immediately after any character satisfying `char::is_whitespace()`, the next non-whitespace Unicode scalar value must be replaced by its complete `char::to_uppercase()` expansion. All other characters remain unchanged.

Every record is an independent text value, so word-boundary state must reset at each record boundary. The implementation incorrectly lets the final state of one record influence the first character of the next.

Repair the implementation and return a complete `solution.rs` exposing the same public API. Use only the Rust standard library. Do not add a `main` function or perform filesystem, network, clock, or random operations.

```rust
pub fn titlecase_records(records: &[&str]) -> Vec<String> {
    let mut output = Vec::with_capacity(records.len());
    let mut at_word_start = true;

    for record in records {
        let mut titled = String::new();
        for ch in record.chars() {
            if ch.is_whitespace() {
                titled.push(ch);
                at_word_start = true;
            } else if at_word_start {
                titled.extend(ch.to_uppercase());
                at_word_start = false;
            } else {
                titled.push(ch);
            }
        }
        output.push(titled);
    }

    output
}
